Found while working k213 and k211 on Windows 2026-11-22 (Windows 11 Pro 26H2, go1.27.0 windows/amd64, native run, not a cross-compile). On main 1ea8353 and f4a906c, `go test ./cmd/launcher/` fails these tests natively on Windows (same set and messages before and after k213, confirmed by unreagent-reviewer in a base worktree):

- TestConsoleNamesAFailedStart, TestPromptNamesAFailedAgentStart, TestUEStartAndRestartFailWhenTheEditorDoesNotStart: exec.Error quotes the program path with %q, so on Windows LastError holds doubled backslashes and strings.Contains(lastErr, path) misses.
- TestRunReplaysTheStartupLinesIntoTheLauncherLog, TestRunWarnsWhenTheEngineAssociationIsNotInstalled (both subtests): the fixture joins an absolute "C:\Program Files\Epic Games\UE_5.9\..." onto t.TempDir(); mkdir fails on Windows.
- TestScriptActionWritesToConfiguredDirectoryAndCleansUpOnSuccess: the script reports its own file path as the working directory, not the directory.

Effect: a Windows run of the suite is red on a clean tree, so a real regression there is hidden among known failures; reviewers currently gate on "no failure beyond base" plus a -skip run. Also noted in k214: the run()-level tests skip on Windows.

